{"name":"Red Bean","hex":"#3d0c02","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red bean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The azuki bean (Vigna angularis), most common in East Asia.","The rice bean (Vigna umbellata)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_bean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red bean","blocks":[{"text":"Red bean is a common name for several varieties of beans and plants and may refer to:"},{"items":["Small red beans, also known as \"Mexican red beans,\" \"Central American red beans,\" and \"New Orleans red beans\"","Adzuki bean, commonly used in Japanese, Korean, and Chinese cuisine, particularly as red bean paste","Kidney bean, a light or dark red variety of Phaseolus vulgaris","Vigna umbellata, a species of legume whose seeds are red","Dysoxylum rufum, a rainforest tree in the Mahogany family","Didymocheton muelleri, a rainforest tree"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_bean"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg/250px-Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg/250px-Bean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABean_Flower_in_Bangladesh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG/250px-Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG/500px-Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG/250px-Lablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALablab_bean_and_bean_flowers.JPG"